{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":6,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1578754484,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDMzNjIwMDQ3Mg=="},"target":"84624e2a2dc2f2a34bfecbb63b614008820b5acb60e9e0c0284575b2caf42fec","message":"Inspired by https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3808#issuecomment-573320479 .\nI think we might want to establish a set of tags to mark \"severity\" or importance (may be mimicing [Debian](https://www.debian.org/Bugs/Developer) but melding top 3 together so we get):\n\n- `severity-critical` - makes it unusable, causes data loss, introduces security vulnerability\n- `severity-important` - major effect on the usability of a package, without rendering it completely unusable to everyone\n- `severity-normal` - the default, majority of issues\n- `severity-minor` - \na problem which doesn't affect the package's usefulness, and is presumably trivial to fix\n- `severity-wishlist` - feature request, and also for any bugs that are very difficult to fix due to major design considerations `FOI:` etc\n- `severity-none` - for all the `FOI: ` and possibly some `Q: ` left unanswered\n\n`critical` and `important` would be release blockers, and all issues should be categorized accordingly.  Then you could easily filter to not miss any important one.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1578754422,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI5NDA2NTUyOTY="},"added":["on hold - input required"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1578758965,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MzMyOTkyMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4011#issuecomment-573329920"},"message":"Given that this model works for Debian, my impulse response is in favor of such categorization.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1578820466,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3MzM5NjIwNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4011#issuecomment-573396207"},"message":"I have created the set of issues. I have renamed the existing 'wishlist' to 'severity-wishlist' in the process.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1578820466,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50Mjk0MTExMzY0NQ=="},"status":2}]}